---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import MadeByKaj from '../../../components/MadeByKaj.astro';
import LiveNotebook from '../../../components/live/LiveNotebook.astro';
import CodeBlockWithCopy from '../../../components/live/CodeBlockWithCopy.astro';
import cell1 from '../../../live-examples/skykit/query-stars-without-three/cell-1.js?raw';
import cell2 from '../../../live-examples/skykit/query-stars-without-three/cell-2.js?raw';
import cell3 from '../../../live-examples/skykit/query-stars-without-three/cell-3.js?raw';
import {
	SKYKIT_BROWSER_ESM_BASE,
	STAR_OCTREE_PROVIDER_VERSION,
	STAR_TREES_VERSION,
} from '../../../config/skykit-live';

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const installCode = `npm install @found-in-space/star-octree-provider@${STAR_OCTREE_PROVIDER_VERSION} @found-in-space/star-trees@${STAR_TREES_VERSION}`;
const browserImportCode = `import {
  OCTREE_DEFAULT,
  createStarOctreeProviderService,
} from "${SKYKIT_BROWSER_ESM_BASE}@found-in-space/star-octree-provider@${STAR_OCTREE_PROVIDER_VERSION}?bundle";
import {
  createObserverShellStrategy,
  createStarCellKey,
  decodeTemperatureK,
} from "${SKYKIT_BROWSER_ESM_BASE}@found-in-space/star-trees@${STAR_TREES_VERSION}?bundle";`;
const importCode = `import {
  OCTREE_DEFAULT,
  createStarOctreeProviderService,
} from '@found-in-space/star-octree-provider';
import {
  createObserverShellStrategy,
  createStarCellKey,
  decodeTemperatureK,
} from '@found-in-space/star-trees';`;
const cells = [
	{
		id: 'provider',
		title: '1. Create The Provider',
		description: 'Open the public render octree and read its descriptor.',
		initialCode: cell1,
	},
	{
		id: 'stream',
		title: '2. Stream Cells',
		description: 'Request position, absolute magnitude, temperature, and StarObjectRef identity.',
		initialCode: cell2,
	},
	{
		id: 'rows',
		title: '3. Inspect Application Rows',
		description: 'Turn streamed cells into rows your app owns, then sort and render a table.',
		initialCode: cell3,
	},
];
---

<Layout
	title="Query stars without Three.js | Found in Space"
	description="Use SkyKit data packages without a 3D renderer by streaming cells into a live table notebook."
>
	<SiteHeader section="Learn & build" />

	<main class="page page--lesson">
		<header class="lesson-hero">
			<nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
				<a href={`${basePath}learn-build/`}>Learn &amp; Build</a>
				<span class="breadcrumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
				<a href={`${basePath}learn-build/skykit/`}>SkyKit</a>
				<span class="breadcrumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
				<span>Query stars without Three.js</span>
			</nav>
			<p class="eyebrow">Lesson 5</p>
			<h1>Query stars without Three.js</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Lessons 1-4 used a viewer helper. Now we peel that away and use the data stream
				directly for lists, maps, games, and custom renderers.
			</p>
		</header>

		<article class="lesson-body prose">
			<section>
				<h2>Learning goal</h2>
				<p>
					This notebook follows the provider-only pattern: create a provider, stream cells,
					listen for deltas, and turn those cells into rows. The required attributes are
					<code>position</code>, <code>magAbs</code>, <code>teffLog8</code>, and
					<code>objectRef</code>.
				</p>
				<p>
					Cells are transport/data units. Rows are app-owned interpretation. The provider does
					not decide what your app is trying to show.
				</p>
				<p>
					The rows from this lesson are plain JavaScript objects. You can draw them with
					Canvas, PixiJS, Phaser, SVG, or your own renderer. SkyKit is not required once you
					choose to own rendering yourself.
				</p>
			</section>
		</article>

		<LiveNotebook
			id="skykit-query-stars"
			title="Stream stars into a table"
			description="Run the cells in order, or edit one cell and rerun from there."
			cells={cells}
		/>

		<article class="lesson-body prose">
			<section class="callout panel">
				<p class="panel__eyebrow">Things to try</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Change <code>limitingMagnitude</code> in cell 2.</li>
					<li>Move <code>observerPc</code> to another location in parsecs.</li>
					<li>Change the sort in cell 3 from brightest stars to coolest stars.</li>
					<li>Add a local filter before <code>slice(0, 40)</code>.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>What changed in the code</h2>
				<p>
					There is no Three.js renderer here. The provider emits deltas such as
					<code>stars/cells-upsert</code>, <code>stars/cells-remove</code>, and
					<code>stars/current</code>. The notebook keeps a local <code>cells</code> array,
					then creates rows by reading coordinate arrays and public star refs.
				</p>
				<p>
					The rendered table intentionally shows a semantic <code>cell key</code>, ordinal,
					x/y/z parsec positions, absolute magnitude, decoded temperature, and whether a
					<code>StarObjectRef</code> is available. It does not expose provider storage offsets.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="source-panel panel">
				<p class="panel__eyebrow">Source and next steps</p>
				<h2>Use the provider examples for deeper diagnostics.</h2>
				<p>
					The SkyKit repository includes a minimal stream example with the same provider,
					cell-delta, and table-rendering structure.
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><a href="https://github.com/Found-in-Space/skykit" rel="noopener noreferrer">SkyKit repository</a></li>
					<li><a href="https://github.com/Found-in-Space/skykit/tree/main/packages/star-octree-provider/examples/minimal-stream" rel="noopener noreferrer">Minimal stream example</a></li>
					<li><a href={`${basePath}learn-build/skykit/star-metadata-sidecars/`}>Next: fetch names and labels with sidecars</a></li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="local-panel panel">
				<h2>Use this in a browser</h2>
				<p>
					For standalone browser examples, use stable, pinned CDN URLs directly. The lesson
					does not introduce version constants or URL helper functions.
				</p>
				<CodeBlockWithCopy code={browserImportCode} label="Browser import" language="js" />

				<h2>Use this locally</h2>
				<p>
					Data-only projects do not need SkyKit or Three.js. Install the focused packages that
					own provider streaming and star interpretation.
				</p>
				<CodeBlockWithCopy code={installCode} label="Install" language="bash" />
				<CodeBlockWithCopy code={importCode} label="Local imports" language="js" />
			</section>
		</article>

		<MadeByKaj />
	</main>
</Layout>
